// arith.jsonl — 8 atoms × 15 probes = 120 probes
// Each line below is a JSON object. Lines starting with // are comments.
// Generated deterministically; ground truths computed in Python.
// Scorer types used: exact_match_string, exact_match_numeric.
//
// Review fixes applied (Explore subagent critique resolved):
//   * exact_integer_op (all 15): added explicit 'no commas, no spaces, no exponent notation'
//     so correct outputs like 9,999,800,001 are not penalised by exact_match_string scorer.
//   * divide.L2.001-005 + divide.L3.005 (sci notation): tightened format spec to forbid
//     '2.0e6' style (require smallest integer mantissa, no trailing zeros).
//   * divide.L3.003: gave the wire mass directly in grams (6000 g) so the probe tests division,
//     not kg->g unit conversion.
//   * percent_of.L3.005: replaced mixture-conservation probe (which dominated by mixture
//     reasoning, not percent_of) with a clean two-step compounded-percentage probe.
//   * compare_quantities.L2.004: replaced date-arithmetic probe (required days-per-month
//     recall) with day-counts already retrieved.
//   * compare_quantities.L1, multiply.L1/L2/L3, divide.L1: diversified surface domains
//     within each cell to remove near-rephrasing.
//   * compare_quantities.L2 (durations): mixed in seconds/hours/days plus min<->h conversion
//     to vary structure beyond 'subtract two H:MM durations'.
//   * multiply.L3.005: rounded float artefact (0.30000000000000004 -> 0.3) in stored expected.
//   * divide.L1.004: corrected operand_form metadata to 'decimals'.
// No declined items.
